        "title": "Ergonomics of Seating",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Seating ergonomics is applied biomechanics: how does the structure of a chair interact with human body geometry to distribute loads, support posture, and minimize fatigue? The engineering problem is harder than it appears because the \"user\" is not a fixed entity."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md#003",
      "path": [
        "08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:furniture:08-ergonomics-seating, git-history:furniture:08-ergonomics-seating]",
        "canonical_path": "furniture/08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md",
        "concepts": "[ergonomics, seating]",
        "current_path": "furniture/08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md",
        "id": "maxim:furniture:ergonomics-seating",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "furniture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ergonomics, seating]",
        "section": "furniture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ergonomics of Seating",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHE SEATING PROBLEM:"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md#004",
      "path": [
        "08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:furniture:08-ergonomics-seating, git-history:furniture:08-ergonomics-seating]",
        "canonical_path": "furniture/08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md",
        "concepts": "[ergonomics, seating]",
        "current_path": "furniture/08-ERGONOMICS-SEATING.md",
        "id": "maxim:furniture:ergonomics-seating",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "furniture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ergonomics, seating]",
        "section": "furniture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ergonomics of Seating",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ANTHROPOMETRIC REALITY:\n  +------------------------------------------+\n  | Human bodies span an enormous range:     |\n  | 5th percentile female → 95th male        |\n  | Seat height range needed: ~380–500mm     |\n  | Seat depth range needed: ~380–480mm      |\n  | A chair optimized for one person         |\n  | will be wrong for many others.           |\n  +------------------------------------------+\n                   |\n                   v\n  +------------------------------------------+\n  | POSTURE REALITY:                         |\n  | Sitting loads the lumbar spine MORE      |\n  | than standing. Slumped sitting: even more.|\n  | No static posture is \"correct\" — the body |\n  | needs variation. The best chair is one   |\n  | that supports many postures, not one.    |\n  +------------------------------------------+\n                   |\n                   v\n  +------------------------------------------+\n  | DESIGN RESPONSE:                         |\n  | 1. Adjustability (multiple parameters)   |\n  | 2. Compliance (chair adapts to body)     |\n  | 3. Encourage movement (synchro-tilt)     |\n  | 4. Match chair to task                   |\n  +------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
